/* =====================================================================
   SEQUOIA PRACTICES . the growth plan library for later life (GWG BLD 733)
   Built for adults 60 and up; anyone 55 and up may choose Sequoia.

   Same shapes as Oak's inline library (oak/index.html), so an app built
   from Oak's index.html swaps Oak's constants for these:
     DOMAIN_DEFS  six parts: key, name, color, group, prompt, restore
                  [[name, line]], strength_msg, growth_steps
     GUIDES       "part|Name": {why, today, build, hard, vary?, adapt?}
                  for the restore practices (Oak's GUIDES)
     G            the same, for the NEW practices (Oak runs
                  Object.assign(GUIDES, G))
     META         part: {Name: [discipline, time, evidence, source url or '']}
     NEW          part: [[name, line]], appended to restore by Oak's code
     EV, DISC     the same codes as Oak
     SRC          source urls used in META
     SHELF        part: [[title, url or '', line]] (Resource shelf)
   Extra for Sequoia (Oak's code ignores these until it reads them):
     FLAGS        "part|Name": {strand: 'move' | 'rest' | 'nourish' (Leaves),
                  levels: ['gentle','moderate','athletic'], seated, bed,
                  safety, chronic (fits life with chronic illness or disability)}
     SOURCES      "part|Name": source ids (shared/gg-sources.js) or
                  {label, href, adapted}, for PX 'sequoia:<practice>'
   adapt (in a guide) is the seated or in-bed version. Oak's guideHtml shows
   why, today, build, hard, vary; one added line shows adapt.
   Edit words in the table below. No dashes; Title Case for practice names.
   ===================================================================== */
